5. THE SELECTION, ROUND 2 (authority: SESSION; ruled_by: Slot A under the owner's standing rule of 26 September 2026, the ruling of
   21 September 2026 and part 19 of 5 October 2026; ruled_on: 5 October 2026)
   (a) and (c) are judged on ONE standard (cx44: rejecting (a) for an unprinted PA transfer while crediting (c)'s was inconsistent): each
     rests on an unprinted PA transfer, so each is at most a PROVISIONAL choice with a supplier validation task. The difference is WHERE
     the unprinted transfer sits: (c) bounds the case's own quantity (DC watts) on the terms of section 4 and leaves the 30 W service on
     one bench row (B-PA1, the module's drain current at 30 W); (a) leaves the case itself on the PA's efficiency at the loop's high end
     (at least 36.5 % at +-0.5 dB) AND the service on a detector chain whose calibration residual no sheet bounds (two bench tasks, one
     of them on the failing case). (b) cannot close the case. RANK: (c) first, (a) second.
   SELECTED: (c), PROVISIONAL: F01 / D-17's row reads PROVISIONAL on B-PA1 (feasibility of the 30 W service under the cap) and B-PA2
     (the dynamics), never closed on printed limits; its dependants read PROVISIONAL too: L9P-F04's closure claim, the PA rail's rows
     (+13V8_PA and +13V8_PAJ at 6.93 A) and board D's loop (R57, R58, R83)
   AFTER cx46 (the second negative on the method, which ends it; kept as given): F01 / D-17 and every dependant (C-ALLTX rev 3 at the
     cap, U13's room, B-PA1's limit, the PA rail's rows) stay PROVISIONAL; the reference's loading through Q551's hold and release and
     the acceptance limits are REMAINING ENGINEERING for the receiving company, never a qualification-only item
   WITHDRAWN (cx44): round 1's fallback "a lower-VGG-wins RF loop for the service floor": an RF loop cannot restore output while the current
     cap binds. If B-PA1 fails (the module needs more than the cap's least for 30 W), the ARRANGEMENT fails (amendment point 4), not a
     requirement: the remaining routes are (R1) raise U13's own limit and the cap with it (R55 lower, J_PA's lead and contacts re-rated: the
     bounded case allows 7.3674 A at the top rail, 0.4415 A more than the cap's top) and (R2) a PA rail at the sheet's 12.5 V with VGG to its 5 V
     condition (U13's divider, board D's VGG band); each would be checked on the same case before adoption. No requirement changes.

